back on may 24th hogwarts legacy  community manager chandler wood posted  on the playstation blog alongside a  social media update for the game which  largely focused on some special features  for the dual sense controller within  that blog post however there were a few  clips that i think some people may have  missed i've seen a few folks in the  comments asking where i found certain  footage for the game so here's  everything they shared within that post  and while most people were excited about  everything we saw there there was a bit  of concern that emerged from the second  clip here which showed off a new  character model in slytherin robes and a  combat scene from the game now there  were two parts that caused some people  to get a little worried and the first is  the robe physics here or lack thereof  notice this section of the gameplay  trailer here and we can see rogue  physics clearly in place compare that to  this brief shot here nowhere near the  same so it was very nice to see chandler  take to twitter this week to address  those concerns by sharing some new  footage of the game confirming that  rogue physics are alive and well in  hogwarts legacy and they aren't going  anywhere this is awesome to see and  personally i would add that i think the  rope physics and movement actually look  much better here than they did even in  the gameplay trailer just a few months  ago and to me this is a fantastic sign  for the progress of the game frankly  it's something i always try and remind  people of when we see footage of these  games it's a vertical slice you just  never know unless it's outright stated  the settings they're running on the  difficulty level what they do and don't  have disabled clearly we don't even see  a hud here which personally i like but i  think the final version of the game will  definitely have some sort of hud by  default now i did mention there were two  concerns that sprang from that brief  clip we saw on the playstation blog post  and the other one is this guy here on  the left side of the screen is it a bug  is it bad ai i don't know one thing we  can say for sure is that it was shown as  part of an unfinished version of the  game guys so i don't think there's any  reason to be concerned about it just yet  at this point i just find it more  humorous than anything else who knows  maybe chandler will share another video  soon addressing that one as well and i  gotta say i think they're continuing to  do a fantastic job with ramping up the  marketing for the game as we move closer  toward launch i love that we're seeing a  steady stream of content even when it's  small updates like this to me i think  fans love the steady updates like this  and i really want to commend chandler  and the team at avalanche for being  willing to share these little details as  things progress we are still keeping our  eyes out for something big later this  summer which was promised by chandler  just a few weeks ago we didn't see any  sign of hogwarts legacy at the summer  game fest and honestly at this point i  think we can pretty much forget about  seeing hogwarts legacy at any of these  industry-wide shows unless it's  something put on by playstation every  single time we've seen a significant  chunk of the game it has been heavily  promoted and pushed by playstation it  started with the ps5 reveal where  hogwarts legacy was officially revealed  as well for the first time then again in  a dedicated state of play just for  hogwarts legacy and finally here in this  recent update from chandler with the  blog post and the video focusing on the  dual sense features now there actually  was a mention of hogwarts legacy on some  new materials from microsoft as well i  think a lot of people may have missed  this one too but if you check out the  official xbox twitter account they  shared this image that has a list of  what's coming to xbox and pc over the  next 12 months on the left you have 2022  and then on the right 2023 but in the  last row on the 2022 side we do indeed  see hogwarts legacy listed there so  confirmation it is still coming to xbox  and it is still on track for 2022. as  for the actual release date we still  don't know when although there have been  some hints within the amazon uk listing  of the hogwarts legacy art book that art  book at least on that uk listing has a  december 6th release date now even if  that is totally accurate that doesn't  necessarily mean that the game is for  sure coming out that day either but i  gotta say honestly that is my personal  guess for when i think hogwarts legacy  is going to release i think december 6  tuesday that is the day at least in my  opinion and fellow hogwarts legacy  youtuber expect a go actually did a  video on this recently and he was kind  enough to ask me to participate among  several other hogwarts legacy creators  that was a super fun video i definitely  encourage you all to check it out you  can see it on the right side of your  screen now and if you're new here don't  forget to hit that subscribe button  before you go as we are closing in on 25  000 subs thank you all for the love as  always thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

